Formalizing the Connectivity Theorem for the Matrix Multiplication Flip Graph in ACL2
Quan Luu, Zeke Medley, Panagiotis Manolios (ACL2 Workshop 2026)

Supporting materials for the paper: an ACL2 proof that the matrix multiplication
flip graph over F2 is strongly connected under flip and plus transformations
(flip-plus-connectivity in main.lisp), together with books relating schemes to
bilinear matrix multiplication algorithms.

Certification
-------------

  cert.pl -j 4 overview-proof.lisp overview-algo.lisp

certifies every book in this directory, in about a minute.  Table 1 of the
paper reports serial certification (cert.pl -j 1 main.lisp) of the connectivity
books only.  For the books in
experiments/, see experiments/README.  Certified with a development snapshot of
ACL2 8.7 (git 98c07036d7) on SBCL 2.6.4, with no trust tags, skip-proofs or
defaxiom.

Overview books
--------------

overview-prelims.lisp   the objects and the statement of the main theorem
overview-proof.lisp     how the main theorem is proved
overview-algo.lisp      schemes and bilinear algorithms

The three restate, with commentary, every definition and theorem the paper
mentions, verbatim from the books in this directory.  Read overview-prelims.lisp
first.

Subfolders
----------

experiments/            the unassisted development and the ACL2s cross-check
                        discussed in the paper's section on working with a
                        language model
